mest November 13 low (tied) of 112 since 1915.","t_rec":"Winslow is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Winslow's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Winslow has set <strong>53 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 88 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">222 record highs</strong>, far more than the 88 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (111). Winslow's all-time high is 110\u00b0F, on July 10, 2021.","t_chg":"Winslow has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 110 complete years: Winslow's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.11 to +0.26), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1915. Winslow's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.28\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.38), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1915.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 9 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Winslow has gotten drier","p_rain":"Winslow's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.19 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.32 to \u22120.06), about \u22122.1 inches since 1915. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 6.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1923 (17.17 in); the driest, 2003 (2.44 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 18 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}